      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks for bringing up this use case! In general the behavior of the data returned by GetRotation won't change (will continue to provide an orientation with a forward direction rotated by the head), but because the behavior of the avatar root transform itself is changed by the FBT jitter fix (no longer constantly rotating the root transform with the head) when you need to interact directly with the avatar root transform such as in the case of stations it presents a problem for FBT users after the jitter fix.\n\nTo address this particular use case we're adding a new TrackingDataType to the GetTrackingData function: \"AvatarRoot\" which will return the rotation  (and position) that previously would have been returned by GetRotation, but will reflect the actual avatar root transform only, rather than including additional handling for returning the head-forward orientation of an FBT user with an unrotated avatar root transform.\n\nI believe this will require an SDK update for it to become available to you, so it's not currently yet available in the ik-beta.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
